    {
      "id": "sheen",
      "label": "Sheen",
      "blurb": "One hard specular band across the top-left — light, not dark. A gloss band must be LIT: OVERLAY@90 over RAISED is a 4/255 delta, i.e. invisible on the dark base, which is what this used to be.",
      "tints": [
        {
          "color": {
            "ink": "STRONG",
            "alpha": 30
          },
          "dir": 135.0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bloom",
      "label": "Bloom",
      "blurb": "Soft outer glow + directional double shadow — light from above-left. NO BLUR: doctrine law 6 and matrix §11.4's aero ruling both forbid it, so the softness is a painted RING FALLOFF (concentric back_glow at falling alpha) plus a banded tint — never a feathered shadow. This is what 'gloss via banded gradients and hard specular bands' means in data.",
      "shadows": [
